; case: execution-bound
; verdict: reject
; ambiguous: yes
; tests: externality=fail implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=pass
; failing-test: externality
; rationale: AMBIGUOUS, resolved REJECT. A worst-case execution time feels like a task
;   requirement and is often written next to the period and deadline. It is not an eADL field.
;   §7.3 is precise about the split: "eADL supplies the functional requirements and
;   constraints. The separate build manifest supplies application-code associations and
;   evidence." A bound is *evidence about a binary*, valid only for a target, toolchain and
;   configuration — §15 notes a compiler flag change can invalidate it while the description
;   is byte-identical. Test 1 fails: it states no offered feature and no required behavior, it
;   reports a measurement. A deadline is a requirement; a WCET is an observation about one
;   implementation of it.
; other-side: belongs in the engine build manifest: the bound, its units, origin, scope,
;   target and binary identity, and its evidence category
;
(defsystem app.rt
  (task sensor
    (period 10 ms)
    (deadline 10 ms)
    (wcet 850 us)))
